  "details": "1. Open VRChat\n\n2. Go into a world\n\n3. Referring the part after downloading, when you begin loading into a instance (Instancing... part with the thumbnail above)\n\nWhen loading into world/instance (after the downloading it), the skybox seems to rotate with the movement of the headset. After a while (I assume after a stage of loading is complete), it freezes and stop rotating. However, this is usually in the wrong orientation.\n\nHas been happening for at least the 4 most recent patches off memory, but is more noticeable with the recent change to the default skybox in the loading screen, as there is a clear horizon line and more features in the sky compared to the blank teal skybox before hand. \n\nCould be affecting PC, but I have not connected a headset up. I am playing on a Quest 3 if that matters.\n\nAppreciate the changes to the login screen and other loading screen though (looks cool :D ).",
